  },
  "description": "LEZREQ crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H74 Dy6 O36 4+,4(C1 F3 O3 S1 1-),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1D (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2D (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3D (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.587-3.930 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.83-115.15°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(μ3-OH)4(μ2-OH)2(L1)8(H2O)6](CF3SO3)4·6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
